  "factor_name": "Downside-volatility share quality",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "clip((sqrt(mean(max(-r,0)^2,40))/std(r,40)), cross_sectional_5pct, cross_sectional_95pct), lag=1",
    "description": "For each asset, measure the share of trailing 40-session volatility attributable to negative returns: downside deviation divided by total return volatility. The signal is lagged one completed session and winsorized cross-sectionally at the 5th and 95th percentiles. Higher values identify assets whose volatility has been more downside-dominated and which historically exhibited positive subsequent cross-sectional returns in this benchmark."
  },
